# Rust Code Guidelines (phoenix)

**Core directive:** You are building a programming language compiler and virtual machine in Rust. Prioritize correctness above all else — a compiler that produces wrong output is worse than one that produces no output. Clarity and maintainability come second. Performance matters but never at the cost of correctness.

This crate uses **Rust standard library only**. Never add dependencies to `Cargo.toml` unless explicitly approved. If something is missing, implement it in-tree. This is a compiler — owning your dependencies is owning your correctness.

