## Post-MVP runtime (reference only)

**Do not implement these until MVP acceptance checklist passes.**

When post-MVP work begins:

- M:N scheduler with fixed worker pool — OS threads spawned only in `src/vm/scheduler.rs`
- Actors identified by `ActorId` (newtype over `u64`); no raw actor pointers across scheduler boundaries
- Each actor: heap state + mailbox (`VecDeque<Message>`) + status (`Running`, `ParkedAwaitIO`, `ParkedAwaitMessage`, `Done`)
- Supervisor trees as explicit data structures with `RestartStrategy`
- Runtime transparency: schedulable I/O visible in types; explicit `@spawn`/`@send` for actor boundaries — see `runtime-transparency.md`
- Compiler passes remain single-threaded; VM scheduler uses `std::thread` and `std::sync` only
- Prefer `std::sync::mpsc` for inter-thread communication; document `Send`/`Sync` on types crossing thread boundaries

