## Additional guidelines

- Prefer `const` / `const fn` for compile-time constants — magic bytes (`PHX0`), version numbers, opcode tags.
- Use `std::mem::take` / `std::mem::replace` to move out of `&mut T` in parser and type checker.
- Prefer `enum` with variants over `bool` + parallel fields for compiler state.
- Use `#[non_exhaustive]` on all Phoenix AST node enums and token enums.
- Gate platform-specific VM code with `#[cfg(target_os = "...")]`.
